{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.TwoRowCapDerived","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TwoRowCapDerived","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.WenzlWeightVanishing","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.FibreDimensionForcesTL"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TwoRowCap.moment_and_schur_routes_agree_of_wenzl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TwoRowCap.moment_and_schur_routes_agree_of_wenzl","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoRowCapDerived.lean#L247-L273","doc":"**The moment route and the Schur route assign the same three-row weight.**\n\nGiven a weight vector satisfying the `H₃(q)` Markov moment equations at\nconvention D's Ocneanu value, its three-row entry equals the convention-D\nSchur weight of `(1,1,1)` — both being zero, each derived without reference to\nthe other.\n\nThe hypotheses are the *union* of the two routes' own hypotheses and nothing\nmore: no step assumes the conclusion of the other route. In particular this is\n**not** a discharge of `markovWeights_eq_jones_of_threeRow_eq_zero`'s `hTL`;\nthat lemma concludes `z·[2]_q = q²`, so feeding it a convention-D weight would\nassume what it proves. The direction here is safe because both sides are\n*consequences* of convention D rather than premises for it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TwoRowCap.schur_route_three_row_eq_zero_of_wenzl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TwoRowCap.schur_route_three_row_eq_zero_of_wenzl","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoRowCapDerived.lean#L222-L227","doc":"The Wenzl/Schur route's value for the three-row weight at `n = 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TwoRowCap.two_one_survives_filter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TwoRowCap.two_one_survives_filter","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoRowCapDerived.lean#L216-L220","doc":"And it keeps something: `(2,1)` has two rows. So the filter is neither\nempty nor everything. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TwoRowCap.exists_three_row_diagram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TwoRowCap.exists_three_row_diagram","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoRowCapDerived.lean#L206-L214","doc":"The filter drops something: `(1,1,1)` has three rows, so it fails\n`colLen 0 ≤ 2`. Together with `conventionD_weight_ne_zero_of_two_rows`\nupstream — which shows the *surviving* diagrams have nonzero weight — this\nmakes the restriction a genuine reduction of the index set that loses no\nmass, rather than a vacuous relabelling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TwoRowCap.twoRow_share_eq_one_of_wenzl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TwoRowCap.twoRow_share_eq_one_of_wenzl","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoRowCapDerived.lean#L182-L199","doc":"**The two-row share of a nonzero Wedderburn sum is exactly `1`.**\n\n`prop:he4-two-row-dominance` asserts this ratio is `≥ 4/5`, with an empirical\n`86.6 %` pinned into a conditional-class instance. At convention D the ratio\nis `1` on the nose, for every braid word and every strand count — there is no\ndominance to measure, because there is no complement.\n\nA measured share strictly below `1` therefore does not refine this bound; it\nrecords a nonzero `≥ 3`-row contribution, which is exactly what convention D\nforbids. Such a measurement is convention-C data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TwoRowCap.threeRowPart_eq_zero_of_wenzl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TwoRowCap.threeRowPart_eq_zero_of_wenzl","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoRowCapDerived.lean#L167-L178","doc":"The complementary statement, stated as the vanishing it really is: the\n`≥ 3`-row part of a Wedderburn sum is zero. Equivalent to\n`traceSum_eq_twoRow_of_wenzl`, but this is the form a \"what is the residual\nshare?\" question wants — the answer is `0`, not \"small\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TwoRowCap.bindingSum_eq_twoRow_of_wenzl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TwoRowCap.bindingSum_eq_twoRow_of_wenzl","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoRowCapDerived.lean#L143-L165","doc":"**The binding sum restricts exactly too, at every `A`.**\n\n  `∑_{μ ∈ s} y_μ · χ_μ · Δ_μ  =  ∑_{μ ∈ s, ℓ(μ) ≤ 2} y_μ · χ_μ · Δ_μ`\n\n`Δ` is arbitrary, so this covers the proved value `Δ_λ = (−1)^{n(λ)}·dim V_λ`\nwithout depending on it. The point is that `Δ_λ` cannot reinstate a dropped\nblock however large it is on many-row diagrams: it multiplies a weight that is\nalready zero.\n\nThis is the formal content of the claim in `def:two-row-stratum` that the\nbinding sum \"does inherit the restriction, at every `A`, exactly\", and of the\n2026-08-09 withdrawal of the opposite reading. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TwoRowCap.traceSum_eq_twoRow_of_wenzl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TwoRowCap.traceSum_eq_twoRow_of_wenzl","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoRowCapDerived.lean#L123-L141","doc":"**The trace sum restricts exactly.**\n\nFor any finite set `s` of Young diagrams and any per-block observable `χ`,\n\n  `∑_{μ ∈ s} y_μ · χ_μ  =  ∑_{μ ∈ s, ℓ(μ) ≤ 2} y_μ · χ_μ`\n\nat convention D. `χ` is arbitrary — the Hoefsmit character is one instance,\nbut nothing here depends on which observable is summed, because the dropped\nterms vanish through the *weight*, whatever multiplies it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TwoRowCap.colLen_le_two_of_massWeight_ne_zero_of_wenzl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TwoRowCap.colLen_le_two_of_massWeight_ne_zero_of_wenzl","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoRowCapDerived.lean#L108-L115","doc":"The contrapositive in the form the sum lemmas consume: a nonzero weight\nforces at most two rows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TwoRowCap.massWeight_eq_zero_of_three_rows_of_wenzl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TwoRowCap.massWeight_eq_zero_of_three_rows_of_wenzl","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoRowCapDerived.lean#L95-L106","doc":"**The mass channel's two-row cap.**\n\nAt convention D — Wenzl level `r = 2`, by `wenzlLevel_conventionD` — a\npartition with three or more rows carries weight exactly zero.\n\nThis is the statement the mass channel posits in several places. It is a\ntheorem: `schurPrincipal_eq_zero_iff` gives it for every `n` and every `λ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}